Package: OligoMetProfiler
Type: Package
Title: Theoretical Metabolite Libraries, Charge Envelopes, and MS/MS
    Fragment Ions for Therapeutic Oligonucleotides
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-08-22
Authors@R: person("Nishikant", "Wase",
    email = "nishikant.wase@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A general-purpose pipeline for in-silico metabolite
    identification of therapeutic oligonucleotides (antisense
    oligonucleotides, siRNA, and related modalities). Generates
    theoretical metabolite libraries (3'/5' exonuclease truncations and
    endonuclease internal fragments), molecular formulas, monoisotopic
    and average masses, negative-ESI charge envelopes with adduct
    variants, isotope patterns, phosphorothioate oxidation series,
    McLuckey MS/MS fragment ions, and PRM inclusion lists for any
    sequence built from DNA, RNA, 2'-O-methyl, 2'-fluoro, MOE, cEt, or
    LNA chemistry with mixed PO/PS backbones -- plus fully custom
    chemistry via dictionary overrides. Four approved oligonucleotide
    therapeutics (nusinersen, inotersen, patisiran, givosiran) ship as
    worked examples spanning the major modality classes; two double as
    the formula engine's regression anchors, reproducing their
    published molecular formulas exactly. Optionally matches the
    theoretical library against uploaded mzML/mzXML or peak-list MS
    data, exports a multi-sheet Excel workbook and HTML/PDF report, and
    writes targeted mass lists formatted for the Thermo Orbitrap
    Exploris Method Editor. A Shiny dashboard (app.R, in the repository
    root) and command-line drivers wrap the same engine.
